{"codec":"JSON-syntax-dictionary-v4","atoms":["\"schema\"","\"identity\"","\"cutoff\"","\"framework\"","\"factor_evidence\"","\"scores\"","\"score_sensitivity\"","\"gates\"","\"history\"","\"historical_vintages\"","\"historical_per_share\"","\"capacity_addition_20251201\"","\"nine_month_sales\"","\"approved_remuneration\"","\"metrics\"","\"incremental_windows\"","\"growth_bridge\"","\"liquidity\"","\"audit\"","\"sources\"","\"assumptions\"","\"model\"","\"classification\"","\"rachit-v3-canonical-1\"","\"name\"","\"symbol\"","\"bse_code\"","\"isin\"","\"exchange\"","\"price\"","\"price_date\"","\"price_confidence\"","\"shares\"","\"lot\"","\"face_value\"","\"Rachit Prints Limited\"","\"RACHIT\"","\"544503\"","\"INE0ZN101029\"","\"BSE SME\"","\"170\"","\"2026-10-19\"","\"Medium; two secondary dated observations, primary BSE tape unavailable\"","4937100","1000","\"10\"","\"2026-10-20\"","\"title\"","\"filename\"","\"sha256\"","\"bytes\"","\"version\"","\"read_in_full\"","\"required_sections\"","\"canonical_factors\"","\"bqs_weights\"","\"gqs_weights\"","\"ias_weights\"","\"Small / Micro-Cap Stock Research Master Prompt v3.0\"","\"Small-Micro-Cap-Stock-Research-Master-Prompt-v3.0.md\"","\"68d4de4255427df276318d0231530b867a453e740c74150e9768bf1387224137\"","72939","\"3.0\"","true","15","13","4","\"GOV\"","\"MOAT\"","\"REV\"","\"DUR\"","\"CAP\"","\"CASH\"","\"BAL\"","\"EXEC\"","\".20\"","\".12\"","\".10\"","\".08\"","\"EARN\"","\".40\"","\".15\"","\"BQS\"","\"R\"","\"D\"","\"P\"","\"L\"","\".25\"","\".35\"","\"factor\"","\"score\"","\"confidence\"","\"rationale\"","\"facts\"","\"strongest_counterevidence\"","\"evidence_ids\"","\"Medium\"","\"Recurring disclosure and control weakness, and concentrated connected-party cash, without demonstrated diversion.\"","\"S1: The audit-trail exception recurs despite unmodified statutory and IFC opinions.\"","\"S1: Elite receivables and advances total ₹4.7972 crore; purchases from CFO-owned Mirahi total ₹1.7544 crore. Commercial terms have not been independently verified.\"","\"S1/S2: AOC2, EPS and tax notes contain inconsistencies. S7 records historical information non-cooperation.\"","\"S16 confirms shareholder approval of the notice remuneration revisions. The voting denominator presentation is inconsistent and is not used to alter issued shares.\"","\"Auditors did not report fraud or default. The RPTs are disclosed, and no material diversion has been substantiated. These facts do not justify an automatic GOV3 or G1 failure.\"","\"S1\"","\"S2\"","\"S3\"","\"S4\"","\"S16\"","\"Customization and repeat customers are useful but contestable, with negotiating power concentrated downstream.\"","\"S3: Seven of the top ten customers had relationships exceeding ten years.\"","\"S3/S8/S9: The Sheela Foam/Kurlon group represented 50.19% of FY25 revenue, while the top five customers represented 82.55%.\"","\"S3: Non-exclusive MoUs contain no guaranteed orders. Standard imported machinery does not establish a proprietary cost or technology advantage.\"","\"Knitted-product growth and the FY25 sales-return rate of 0.28% demonstrate customer acceptance. The business is not wholly undifferentiated.\"","\"S8\"","\"S9\"","7","\"The preferred five-year comparable revenue CAGR, FY21–FY26, falls in the 15–20% band. No trajectory adjustment.\"","\"S4/S3/S2/S1: Operating revenue rose from ₹23.9094 crore to ₹53.2399 crore at an unchanged standalone perimeter, with no acquisition identified.\"","\"The FY23–FY26 three-year cross-check falls in the same 15–20% band.\"","\"Manufacturing dominates the FY26 addition. S15 reports approximate nine-month quantity growth of 19.42% and value growth of 28.13%; product-mix and full-year price/volume attribution remain unavailable. TAM earns no score bonus.\"","\"The pandemic-affected FY21 base and FY23 stock-record limitation reduce confidence. Connected-party sales contribute to the latest increment.\"","\"S15\"","5","\"There is real access to mattress-fabric demand, limited by customer concentration and unverified economics of further capacity.\"","\"S3: Knitted-fabric capacity grew and reported FY25 utilization was 100%.\"","\"S14: Six machines were commissioned in December 2025, increasing stated daily knitted-fabric capacity from 6,300 to 9,300 metres.\"","\"S1/S3: The separate 12-machine IPO object was unspent at March 2026; its quoted price expired in October 2025 and completion has not been verified.\"","\"The completed six-machine cohort, FY26 PPE investment and manufactured-sales growth demonstrate expansion activity. No blanket assertion that every growth program stalled is justified.\"","\"S14\"","null","\"Low\"","\"NS: Additional-capital returns cannot be separated reliably into installed cohorts, working-capital reclassifications and trough recovery.\"","\"Three- and five-year NOPAT/capital bridges are provided as diagnostics, not clean unit returns.\"","\"FY26 book capital grew sharply while operating EBIT improved only modestly.\"","\"FY23 stock records, FY24 cash/debt vintages and non-operating balances impair precise capital attribution.\"","\"Older assets and customers generated a strong FY24–FY25 profit recovery. This does not prove that all new investment destroys value.\"","3","\"Persistent weak realization, not just one expansion year: five-year conversion is weak under both original and favorable restated CFO presentations.\"","\"FY23 CFO was negative; FY25 CFO was near zero despite ₹4.56 crore PAT; FY26 CFO was negative ₹3.60 crore.\"","\"FY24 positive CFO included stock/advance releases and classification changes, rather than a demonstrated steady cash engine.\"","\"S1: Aged and disputed receivables remain classified as good, alongside substantial supplier and related-party advances.\"","\"FY26 investment could produce later collections, and FY24 did include genuine working-capital release. Nevertheless capex does not explain negative CFO, and the multi-year pattern supports the GQS cap at5.\"","\"NS: Actual entry cash and confirmed bank availability are missing. The March balance sheet alone cannot establish survival.\"","\"S1: Available cash before further haircut is ₹0.2275 crore, against annual term principal of ₹2.5246 crore.\"","\"S1: The ₹4.4 crore IPO deposit is earmarked; the ₹1.9657 crore SBI deposit is pledged; drawn debt is ₹10.8979 crore.\"","\"No automatic access to an undrawn facility, released collateral, subsidy or promoter rescue is assumed.\"","\"Post-IPO equity of ₹34.8962 crore, moderate accounting leverage and no reported default argue against claiming proven insolvency.\"","\"Mixed delivery: demonstrated product scaling and a completed six-machine cohort, against the delayed IPO object and weak cash delivery.\"","\"S3/S14: Knitted output grew from 1.221 to 1.885 million metres in FY23–FY25; six further machines were commissioned on 1 December 2025.\"","\"S1/S3: The RHP indicated FY26 procurement for the 12-machine IPO object, versus zero capex-object utilization at March 2026. The completed six cannot be mapped to that object without invoices and funding records.\"","\"FY26 manufacturing growth did not deliver current-share earnings or cash progress.\"","\"S15 corroborates nine-month sales quantity growth, but does not establish realized output or utilization by machine cohort.\"","\"The completed six machines increased stated daily capacity by 3,000 metres. Together with ₹9.10 crore FY26 cash capex, this supports EXEC5 rather than the earlier incomplete-evidence score of 4. Realized line-level utilization and cohort returns remain unknown.\"","\"Profits are mainly operating, but latest per-share progress is mixed and normalization matters.\"","\"FY26 other income of ₹0.278 crore is small relative to ₹6.210 crore PBT; gains are not the dominant source.\"","\"FY26 revenue rose27.7% but PAT only0.44%, as depreciation and financing costs increased.\"","\"The IPO increased the current share denominator36.08%. Current-share EPS is ₹9.28 versus FY25 closing-share EPS of ₹12.57.\"","\"The FY23–FY25 operating-profit recovery and current interest coverage support real earnings. Weak cash alone is not evidence of fabricated profit.\"","\"NS: A supported base-case investor return cannot be established without actual entry liquidity and financing evidence.\"","\"The five-year cash models are explicitly conditional.\"","\"Every unfunded breach suppresses ordinary IRR; optional recapitalization is never called committed.\"","\"The indicative ₹170 secondary price does not establish executable entry.\"","\"An illustrative surviving path may meet some hurdles. That result cannot fill an actual evidence gap.\"","\"Material permanent-impairment risk exists under credible linked customer, collection and margin stress.\"","\"Customer-group and connected-counterparty concentrations interact with thin available cash.\"","\"The bear and slower-collection models quantify unfunded gaps and bounded recapitalization.\"","\"Book equity is not a liquid recovery floor: stock, plant, advances and aged receivables can lose value together.\"","\"Moderate drawn leverage and recent primary capital provide a buffer. Documented bank headroom could improve resilience; certain failure is not claimed.\"","\"NS: Reverse expectations depend on unsupported actual entry cash, capacity ramp and terminal economics.\"","\"Revenue-growth scans retain every failed candidate path.\"","\"Terminal EV is earned from FCFF and capital requirements, not automatic P/E rerating.\"","\"Reported P/E is a cross-check, not a substitute for intrinsic value.\"","\"Mid-teens historical revenue growth and recent investment can create value if cash conversion improves.\"","\"NS: Primary BSE20/60-session traded values and current restrictions are missing.\"","\"S5 supports the1000-share reference lot and current shares, not a BSE trading series.\"","\"Secondary19October ₹170/2000-share observations cannot replace60 verified sessions.\"","\"The ₹5 lakh reference cannot be represented exactly by whole lots: two cost ₹3.4 lakh and three ₹5.1 lakh.\"","\"The stock has reported trading. Missing NSE issuer rows do not prove suspension or zero BSE liquidity.\"","\"S5\"","\"S6\"","\"S13\"","\"GQS\"","\"IAS\"","\"terms\"","\"known_contribution\"","\"coverage\"","\"missing_weight\"","\"raw\"","\"final\"","\"uncapped_lower\"","\"uncapped_upper\"","\"lower\"","\"upper\"","\"caps\"","\"rank_eligible\"","\"display\"","\"weight\"","\"contribution\"","\"0.20\"","\"0.80\"","\"0.12\"","\"0.84\"","\"0.10\"","\"0.50\"","\"0.30\"","\"0.08\"","\"0.40\"","\"3.64\"","\"3.84\"","\"5.64\"","false","\"2.80\"","\"1.00\"","\"0.15\"","\"0.75\"","\"4.85\"","\"0.85\"","\"5.00\"","\"6.35\"","\"5\"","\"Persistent poor cash realization: maximum 5\"","\"dependency_tight_lower\"","\"dependency_tight_upper\"","\"0.25\"","\"0.35\"","\"0.60\"","\"1.40\"","\"8.60\"","\"2.1100\"","\"7.5100\"","\"delta\"","-1","\"3.44\"","\"5.44\"","\"3\"","\"GOV <= 3: maximum 3\"","\"GOV3wouldactivategovernancecap;if justified. OtherwiseHold—unresolved, notrankingeligible.\"","1","\"4.04\"","\"5.84\"","\"id\"","\"status\"","\"reason\"","\"G1\"","\"Conditional\"","\"Recurring control/disclosure weakness and connected-party cash exposure. No substantiated diversion or serious minority abuse established.\"","\"G2\"","\"Hold — unresolved\"","\"Historical cash vintages, FY23 stock records, recurring audit-trail limitation and financial-note inconsistencies require clarification.\"","\"G3\"","\"Actual March-to-entry cash and bank availability are unknown. A simulated floor breach is not an actual default; optional rescue is not committed.\"","\"G4\"","\"No primary BSE20/60-session series or current restrictions. The NSE reference is not a BSE tape.\"","\"year\"","\"revenue\"","\"other_income\"","\"pbt\"","\"finance\"","\"da\"","\"pat\"","\"cfo\"","\"capex\"","\"ppe\"","\"cwip\"","\"ar\"","\"inventory\"","\"advances\"","\"other_ca\"","\"payables\"","\"other_cl\"","\"provisions\"","\"equity\"","\"debt\"","\"c